{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Where's that girl with the red dress on? Some folks calls her [D7]Dinah;
Stole my heart away from me, way down in [G]Louisiana.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Take Me back to Tulsa, I'm too young to [D7]marry;
Take me back to Tulsa, I'm too young to [G]marry.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Would I like to go to Tulsa? Boy I sure would
Let me off at Orchard, I’ll walk down to greenwood
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
There ain’t much to this little song, and really we don’t care
We’re gonna do it anyway because we go right by there
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
We always wear a great big smile, we never do look sour
Travel all ov’r the country, playin’ by the hour
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Take Me back to Tulsa, I'm too young to [D7]marry;
Take me back to Tulsa, I'm too to young [G]to wed thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
Alternate lines
Oh, walk and talk suzy, walk and talk suzy.
Walk and talk suzy, walk and talk suzy.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
I went to the Railroad, laid my head down on the track.
I thought about that girl of mine and I gradually eased it back.
{end_of_verse}
